  "design_section": "7.17",
  "design_notes": [
    "The column is headed \"Data rate (game)\", so stats are game values. The \"Fact\" column is stored in twin. Section 7.2.1 says the satellite reuses this table.",
    "Relay network subscription has \"Continuous coverage\" in the data-rate column and \"—\" for pointing: it has no data rate and no pointing value, only continuous_coverage. The design lists it beside the radios and does not say whether it replaces a radio or is bought on top of one. Open design question.",
    "\"$3 M per mission\" (relay) is the only cost in the table and is stored as cost_M 3.",
    "Laser \"new tech\" is stored as maturity new, as for the engines whose drawback reads \"new tech\". There is no reliability for the band to apply to.",
    "\"Needs attitude control\" (X-band) is a flag, not a requires_part rule: attitude control is voted only in the satellite Payload Bay, so a hard rule could not be met in other contracts. Ka-band and laser demand finer pointing but the table does not repeat the drawback for them.",
    "\"Rain fade\" and \"Clouds block it\" have no numbers; they are flags.",
    "Facts: F34 (TDRS) and F35 (laser comms) are the fact-bank entries of this section. F09 (Deep Space Network sites) is attached to X-band because its fact line is about the Deep Space Network; the bank ties F09 to MG-13.",
    "No option is restricted to a contract. The relay subscription has no model path: it is a service, not hardware."
  ],
